From 7157000000000000000000000000000000000009 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RistOS Build <build@ristos.org>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] rist: do not pull LocalContactsBackup into the image

Seedvault lists LocalContactsBackup (package app.grapheneos.backup.contacts)
in its `required:`. aosp/rist.mk names LocalContactsBackup in
ETC.RistAssistant.OVERRIDES, but that filter only reaches modules Make
expands itself; a module that arrives through another module's `required:`
is installed anyway. rist.2026100700 shipped both
system/app/LocalContactsBackup/LocalContactsBackup.apk and
system/etc/default-permissions/default-permissions_app.grapheneos.backup.contacts.xml.

Drop the edge at its source. Seedvault itself (com.stevesoltys.seedvault)
is unchanged and keeps working; only its contacts backup goes, which is
what the override list already intended.

tools/check_debrand.py fails the release if either file, or any APK whose
package is a GrapheneOS package outside the keep-list, is still in
target_files.

Apply from the packages/apps/Seedvault git project with `git am`;
independent of the other patches. Context is from the GrapheneOS tag
2026091900 (Seedvault 4b9bf6220b1b).
---
 Android.bp | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Android.bp b/Android.bp
index c0b118d..430f2a5 100644
--- a/Android.bp
+++ b/Android.bp
@@ -61,7 +61,6 @@ android_app {
     certificate: "platform",
     privileged: true,
     required: [
-        "LocalContactsBackup",
         "com.stevesoltys.backup_allowlist",
         "com.stevesoltys.backup_default-permissions",
         "com.stevesoltys.backup_privapp_allowlist"
